            <ArticleTitle>Anterior Segment Injury by a High-Power Handheld Blue Laser Device.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1080/09273948.2017.1327603</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="PURPOSE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To report a case of severe anterior segment inflammation secondary to exposure to a high-power blue laser device.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">Case report.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">A 14-year-old male presented with redness, pain and decreased vision in his left eye after exposure to blue laser. Examination indicated severe conjunctival injection associated with 4+ cells in the anterior chamber with fibrinous reaction. The posterior pole was normal.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Blue laser devices are easily available through the Internet. These devices can cause devastating ocular injuries. National safety guidelines are required to regulate use.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
